WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:36.670
[Beast Pirates gasping]

3
00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:39.620
<b>The Sake I Brewed to Drink With You</b>

4
00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:39.340
[screams]

5
00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:47.850
[gasps]
The whole island
floating in the sky?

6
00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:52.890
This is like a dream.
No! A nightmare!

7
00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:57.230
How can we hope to defeat Kaido?
His strength is too great!

8
00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:02.570
[QUEEN]
What? Why are you here? No way!

9
00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:04.820
[PIRATES grunting, panting]

10
00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:06.750
[PIRATES screaming]

11
00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:06.750
[QUEEN]
Marco the Phoenix!

12
00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:08.940
<b>Marco the Phoenix

Former Whitebeard Pirate</b>

13
00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:09.080
We need a lot of fire, now!

14
00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:12.160
In that case, here you go!

15
00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:15.660
[gasps, screams]
Hot, hot, hot!

16
00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:16.910
[Omasa yells] [both gasp]

17
00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:18.250
What are you doing?

18
00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:18.330
No, no! It's hot! I'm burning!

19
00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:19.910
Oh no, it's hot! It's so hot!

20
00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:21.710
I'm burning from the inside out!

21
00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:21.320
[PIRATES groaning]

22
00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:24.160
Damn it! Is this
some kind of joke to you?

23
00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:27.280
We thought you were an ally
and this is what you do?

24
00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:28.740
Explain yourself.

25
00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:30.500
[ZORO]
Or die!

26
00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:36.040
Boy, somebody has
a real short fuse.

27
00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:38.210
[Chopper gasping]

28
00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:41.460
All right, don't worry, Chopper!
I'll put it out for you!

29
00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:46.090
Ah, my arm bones! I'm burning!

30
00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:49.510
Or not? Well, this is unique.

31
00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:52.220
It's all right,
my friend! Relax!

32
00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:53.850
But the fire!

33
00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:54.460
[gasps]

34
00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:56.810
Oh wait. Uh... I'm not burning.

35
00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:57.940
I'm totally okay!

36
00:02:57.940 --> 00:03:01.440
It's warm and comfy
like a perfect summer day.

37
00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:03.230
It feels so nice.

38
00:03:03.230 --> 00:03:04.690
[TRISTAN, MIYAGI]
– Dr. Chopper!
– Dr. Chopper!

39
00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:06.070
[gasps]

40
00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:08.070
We're ready to begin
production of the antibodies,

41
00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:10.700
if you-gara would come this way!

42
00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:12.050
<b>Miyagi, Mink Doctor</b>
<b>Tristan, Mink Nurse</b>

43
00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:13.690
[Ice Oni growling]

44
00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:16.110
My goodness!
It's a swarm of Ice Oni!

45
00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:17.320
[Tristan gasps]

46
00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:20.660
[CHOPPER]
Miyagi! Tristan!
Run for it! Hurry!

47
00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:23.280
Might as well get
'em all, I guess!

48
00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:28.460
[MARCO]
Phoenix Pyreapple!

49
00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:32.840
[all groan]

50
00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:34.420
[Omasa groans]

51
00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:38.800
[Beast Pirate B screaming]

52
00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:41.340
Wait, this is kind
of nice, actually.

53
00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:49.490
[Samurai G groaning]
I can feel
the chill melting away already!

54
00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:53.650
[groaning]
What was I doing?

55
00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:55.360
Are you all right?

56
00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:56.480
You had me worried there,

57
00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:59.820
but it seems you
came to your senses!

58
00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:02.060
You sure scared me!

59
00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:05.570
The only thing I did was
raise their body temperature.

60
00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:06.900
The second their
stamina runs out,

61
00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:09.950
they'll start going berserk,
just like before.

62
00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:12.950
So you better use the time
while you've still got it.

63
00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:14.700
[gasps]

64
00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:18.460
You're a lifesaver!

65
00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:21.290
A little time is all I needed!

66
00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:27.000
Tristan, Miyagi!
You okay over there?

67
00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.300
Yes, it seems!

68
00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:29.880
Just shaken up, is all!

69
00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:32.510
All right then,
let's get down to it!

70
00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:35.600
Since we're clear for now,
we'll get right to work!

71
00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:36.930
Thanks a bunch!

72
00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:39.910
Guess they're using space
in that tower! Okay!

73
00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:45.000
[growls]
I'll kill you!

74
00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.080
Stupid bird and stupid raccoon,

75
00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:49.580
playing doctor and
messing up all my stuff!

76
00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:49.700
[both gasp]

77
00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:51.040
Hey, you morons!

78
00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:52.120
You don't really
think he's gonna

79
00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:53.710
spare his own enemies, do you?

80
00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:54.010
He's

81
00:04:54.010 --> 00:04:55.680
He's gonna save his buddies

82
00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:57.660
and they're gonna
finish you off!

83
00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:01.000
I dunno. Our friends
are gonna die.

84
00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.920
That's right, they'll die!

85
00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:06.420
Then you're all gonna die
unless you get rid of that pest

86
00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:08.690
and bring back
my antibody immediately!

87
00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:09.940
Simple enough.

88
00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:11.610
I can lend a hand
without much effort,

89
00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:13.740
but it seems like
we're overstaffed.

90
00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:15.570
Roronoa, listen up!

91
00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:16.660
I think you might be better off

92
00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:18.990
fighting Kaido on
the roof right now.

93
00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:21.240
[gasps]

94
00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:23.660
Having trouble getting up there?

95
00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:25.580
Why not let me fly you, then?

96
00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:26.880
You Straw Hats are
way too strong

97
00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:29.040
to be dealing with
a buncha small fries.

98
00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:30.750
[all gasp]

99
00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:32.590
But we can't leave yet!

100
00:05:32.590 --> 00:05:34.340
We still have to
protect Chopper!

101
00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:36.090
[Hyogoro grunts]

102
00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:38.010
[Beast Pirates groan]

103
00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:40.140
It's fine, Mister Skeleton.

104
00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:41.600
We can handle this.

105
00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:44.940
We won't let any harm
come to Mister Raccoon.

106
00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:46.770
You have my word!

107
00:05:49.260 --> 00:05:49.690
Let's

108
00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:52.530
Let's give it our best!
We've got this!

109
00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:57.370
[panting]

110
00:05:57.370 --> 00:06:00.700
Hold up! I'm not
done with you yet!

111
00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:01.830
[all gasp]

112
00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:05.170
[gasps]
Apoo!

113
00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:06.580
Check it!

114
00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:10.170
You punks better give me back
that antibody or else!

115
00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:15.470
[panting]
They'll kill me
if I don't get it.

116
00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:16.640
I can't lose now.

117
00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:19.760
I'm fighting for
my life, damn it!

118
00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:21.060
Seriously?

119
00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:23.230
Very well. Have at you!

120
00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:25.850
One more enemy,
then we'll be on our way.

121
00:06:25.850 --> 00:06:27.900
[yells]

122
00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:30.940
Flee to the tower, Mister
Raccoon. We're all right!

123
00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:36.620
[roars]

124
00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:36.700
[Beast Pirate I screams]

125
00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:37.820
[gasps]

126
00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:44.460
[Beast Pirate I screams]

127
00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:45.000
Well, that's new.

128
00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:49.090
[BEAST PIRATES]
Apoo, no!

129
00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:50.930
<b>X Drake
Formerly of the Soaring Six
Ancient Saur-Saur Fruit: Allosaurus</b>

130
00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:52.130
I'll beat your scaly ass
into the ground!

131
00:06:52.130 --> 00:06:53.590
He betrayed us?

132
00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:56.760
So, does that mean we should
attack him to protect Apoo?

133
00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:00.220
[Apoo groans]

134
00:07:03.740 --> 00:07:07.990
[DRAKE]
Roronoa Zoro, if you
can trust me as your ally,

135
00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:10.830
let me handle this and go ahead!

136
00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:14.920
Well, if nothing else,
it looks like you've got

137
00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:18.040
a knack for betting
on the right horse.

138
00:07:18.210 --> 00:07:21.880
<b>4th Floor



Inside

the Castle</b>

139
00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:23.680
If I had to guess

140
00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:26.230
I'd wager that he sensed
a powerful enemy nearby

141
00:07:26.230 --> 00:07:28.480
and he's holding them off
on the third floor.

142
00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:29.900
I didn't think of that!

143
00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:32.900
Guess my Observation
Haki's still weak.

144
00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:36.030
He can't be far from here,
but I can't sense Sanji at all!

145
00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:37.400
[Jinbe laughs]

146
00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:43.150
Did you feel something
just now? Enemies?

147
00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:46.320
Indeed. Many of them.

148
00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:49.240
Nearby. Ready to strike.

149
00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:52.330
It seems they're quite
formidable as well.

150
00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:58.300
[Who's Who Pirates cackling]

151
00:07:58.300 --> 00:08:00.340
One of us is going to
have to stay behind

152
00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:02.300
and keep these foes occupied.

153
00:08:02.300 --> 00:08:04.300
[Who's Who Pirates cackling]

154
00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:07.140
You go on ahead.
I'll draw their attention.

155
00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:08.210
Suck

156
00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:16.330
Launcher!

157
00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:26.570
<b>Right-Brain Tower

Inside the Dome</b>

158
00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:30.890
[FRANKY]
Now that is how
you make a mess of things!

159
00:08:31.260 --> 00:08:34.350
General Cannon!

160
00:08:34.350 --> 00:08:36.600
Damn it! Get back!

161
00:08:41.940 --> 00:08:43.320
Huh?

162
00:08:44.940 --> 00:08:46.400
[SASAKI]
You think I'm just gonna

163
00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:49.030
let you blow everything up?

164
00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:54.240
[SASAKI]
Don't push it, little robot!

165
00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:58.500
Wow, that is one hell of
an upgrade, brother!

166
00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:05.800
[FRANKY]
I love me a good dinosaur!

167
00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:09.240
<b>Sasaki
Soaring Six
Ancient Saur-Saur Fruit: Triceratops</b>

168
00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:10.890
[FRANKY]
A triceratops, huh?

169
00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:12.050
[SASAKI]
What of it?

170
00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:16.020
Dinosaurs are the strongest
creatures that ever lived!

171
00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:19.900
[SASAKI]
You're gonna get
scrapped, you giant tin can!

172
00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:22.200
[FRANKY]
Who you calling a tin can?

173
00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:25.450
Wapometal never
loses its luster!

174
00:09:25.450 --> 00:09:27.950
[yells]

175
00:09:27.950 --> 00:09:30.460
[Franky grunts]

176
00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:34.840
[Franky yells]

177
00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:36.880
[Page One, Ulti grunt]

178
00:09:38.850 --> 00:09:44.560
<b>Outside

the Onigashima

Dome</b>

179
00:09:42.590 --> 00:09:45.010
[SAMURAI M]
It's the Tobi Roppo!

180
00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:48.360
<b>Ulti
Soaring Six
Ancient Saur-Saur Fruit: Pachycephalosaurus</b>
<b>Page One
Soaring Six
Ancient Saur-Saur Fruit: Spinosaurus</b>

181
00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:56.820
[PAGE ONE]
Little pests. Where did they go?

182
00:09:56.820 --> 00:09:59.780
[ULTI]
I'm ever-ever
so cross, brother dear!

183
00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:03.240
Why, I just might
crush that bitch's head

184
00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:05.660
into a thousand little pieces!

185
00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:08.490
[screeches]

186
00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:18.510
<b>Banquet Hall

3rd Floor

Inside the Castle</b>

187
00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:28.200
[gasps]
Damn it! What is this?

188
00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:30.250
[gasps]
Get this crap off me!

189
00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:33.460
[BLACK MARIA]
Don't tire yourself out already.

190
00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:37.300
After all, the fun's
just starting.

191
00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:38.840
[Sanji gasps]

192
00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:41.090
[BLACK MARIA]
Are you a gentleman, or not?

193
00:10:41.090 --> 00:10:45.430
You said you loved me.
Was that a lie?

194
00:10:46.670 --> 00:10:49.670
<b>Black Maria
Soaring Six
Ancient Spider-Spider Fruit: Rosamygale Grauvogeli</b>

195
00:10:49.810 --> 00:10:51.020
[gasps]

196
00:10:51.020 --> 00:10:53.440
[Gifters giggling]

197
00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:56.730
[Black Maria chuckles]
I've been
looking for a cute pet like you.

198
00:10:56.730 --> 00:10:59.110
I think I just might
keep you forever!

199
00:10:59.110 --> 00:11:01.950
I already told you.
I have to go!

200
00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:05.530
My captain is counting
on me! And yet...

201
00:11:05.530 --> 00:11:08.160
[all chuckling]

202
00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:09.370
[SANJI]
There's women.

203
00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:13.670
Everywhere I look,
ladies, ladies, ladies!

204
00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:20.130
Could this be... heaven?

205
00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:22.340
[Gifter C gasps]
I think the man's lost his mind.

206
00:11:22.340 --> 00:11:24.050
[Black Maria chuckles]
Yes, well.

207
00:11:24.050 --> 00:11:26.050
He's lucky he's
still good-looking.

208
00:11:26.050 --> 00:11:28.140
[yells]

209
00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:29.460
<b>Big Cat Cafe

4th Floor</b>

210
00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:31.130
[sighs]
Of course.

211
00:11:31.130 --> 00:11:34.340
Straw Hat and his crew managed
to break through our forces.

212
00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:36.120
[Who's-Who Pirate A groans]

213
00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:36.430
That's no good for Kaido.

214
00:11:36.430 --> 00:11:37.970
This is a real mess.

215
00:11:37.970 --> 00:11:41.300
[Who's-Who Pirates chuckle]

216
00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:43.670
Could you hold on for a sec?

217
00:11:43.670 --> 00:11:46.680
I don't like you
picking on my underlings.

218
00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:48.310
<b>Who's-Who
Soaring Six
Ancient Cat-Cat Fruit: Saber-Toothed Tiger</b>

219
00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:48.290
[laughs]

220
00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:49.670
[OTAMA]
Hihimaru!

221
00:11:50.720 --> 00:11:53.430
I thought a former warlord
would show some restraint,

222
00:11:53.430 --> 00:11:57.270
but you came out swinging
like a common thug.

223
00:11:57.270 --> 00:11:57.320
[JINBE]
I'll have you know,
I'm the helmsman

224
00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:59.020
Because I'm the helmsman
of the Straw Hats!

225
00:11:59.020 --> 00:12:00.940
of the Straw Hat Pirates now.

226
00:12:00.940 --> 00:12:04.110
If you want to speak of manners,
then use my proper title!

227
00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:06.950
My mistake. It has been a while.

228
00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:08.990
But I saw you when
you were a Warlord,

229
00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:11.280
so that stuck with me.

230
00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:12.740
You what?

231
00:12:12.740 --> 00:12:13.280
[Who's-Who Pirates chuckle]

232
00:12:13.280 --> 00:12:15.360
Well, enough about all that.

233
00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:18.450
[JINBE]
Out with it. Who are you?

234
00:12:18.450 --> 00:12:21.320
Who indeed. I do wonder.

235
00:12:21.320 --> 00:12:25.870
I'll find out soon either way
after I tear off that mask.

236
00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:30.750
[chuckles]
Not that easy, pal.

237
00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:32.500
It's a storehouse.

238
00:12:31.110 --> 00:12:33.650
<b>Forbidden Storehouse

Inside the Dome</b>

239
00:12:36.310 --> 00:12:36.670
[SHINOBU]
I

240
00:12:37.050 --> 00:12:39.140
[YAMATO]
But I doubt
anyone will come here,

241
00:12:39.140 --> 00:12:41.530
[panting] so we can hide at least.

242
00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:44.120
[MOMONOSUKE]
Uh, do you know what this is?

243
00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:46.040
[YAMATO]
A statue of a dragon.

244
00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:48.170
It used to be at the
entrance of the island,

245
00:12:48.170 --> 00:12:51.790
but my friend broke it,
so they tossed it in here.

246
00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:53.340
[MOMONOSUKE]
Your friend?

247
00:12:54.930 --> 00:12:57.310
Several years ago,

248
00:12:57.310 --> 00:13:00.520
he came here in hopes of
killing my father.

249
00:13:09.900 --> 00:13:12.490
[ACE]
That's weird. No one's here.

250
00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:18.480
[Yamato yells]

251
00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:21.820
[Yamato gasps]

252
00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:23.700
Intruder alert!

253
00:13:24.410 --> 00:13:26.740
I'm here for Kaido, not for you!

254
00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:28.740
[grunts]

255
00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:32.960
[Beast Pirates scream]

256
00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:34.210
[CORNELIA]
What now, Ace?

257
00:13:34.210 --> 00:13:36.630
[ACE]
I got this.
You guys save the kids.

258
00:13:36.630 --> 00:13:37.920
[SKULL]
On it!

259
00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:39.210
[CORNELIA]
Good luck!

260
00:13:41.680 --> 00:13:43.970
You're persistent, aren't ya?

261
00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:48.890
[Ace yells]

262
00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:52.100
Who the hell are you?
Tell me your name!

263
00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:54.020
You tell me yours!

264
00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:55.520
[grunts]

265
00:13:58.020 --> 00:13:59.610
My name's Ace!

266
00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:01.550
And I'm not leaving
till I take Kaido's head!

267
00:14:01.550 --> 00:14:06.300
[CORNELIA]
I found them!
Over here, hurry!

268
00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:09.950
[Ace yells]

269
00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:13.000
Don't be afraid.
We came here to rescue you.

270
00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:14.960
Come on. Let's get you
out of here.

271
00:14:14.960 --> 00:14:20.260
[Ace grunting]

272
00:14:14.960 --> 00:14:19.050
[Ace yells]

273
00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:16.920
[girls gasp]

274
00:14:24.180 --> 00:14:26.180
[ACE]
You're pretty strong.

275
00:14:31.370 --> 00:14:34.040
[CORNELIA]
Ace! We have the kids
with us, everyone's okay.

276
00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:37.290
But the bad news is there's
no sign of Kaido anywhere here!

277
00:14:37.290 --> 00:14:38.410
[ACE]
What?

278
00:14:38.410 --> 00:14:40.710
My father is off
on an expedition.

279
00:14:40.710 --> 00:14:44.920
And not only him,
his officers are gone, too!

280
00:14:44.920 --> 00:14:46.000
Your father?

281
00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:47.130
[all gasp]

282
00:14:47.130 --> 00:14:48.630
So Kaido has a daughter

283
00:14:48.630 --> 00:14:51.390
and he left her in charge
of the whole place?

284
00:14:52.840 --> 00:14:54.800
I am Yamato!

285
00:14:54.800 --> 00:14:58.100
Now I think it's time we all
stop this pointless violence!

286
00:14:58.100 --> 00:15:00.350
If you have time
to wonder who I am,

287
00:15:00.350 --> 00:15:02.020
get out of here right now,

288
00:15:02.020 --> 00:15:05.230
and take those children
back to their families!

289
00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:09.780
I'd be happy to do just that.

290
00:15:09.780 --> 00:15:12.530
But will Kaido forgive you
for letting us go?

291
00:15:12.530 --> 00:15:16.290
I have no obligation to
protect this island for him.

292
00:15:16.290 --> 00:15:19.250
[gasps]

293
00:15:18.420 --> 00:15:20.920
[chuckles]

294
00:15:24.670 --> 00:15:27.300
Ready? We'll have you
back home in no time!

295
00:15:27.300 --> 00:15:29.640
Don't worry! Your families
are waiting for you!

296
00:15:29.640 --> 00:15:30.890
Yes, of course.

297
00:15:30.890 --> 00:15:33.220
Thank you. Thank you. I mean it!

298
00:15:33.220 --> 00:15:34.870
Are you sure you wanna
stay here, Ace?

299
00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:35.350
you wanna pay me back,

300
00:15:35.350 --> 00:15:36.770
We're heading back
to the mainland,

301
00:15:36.770 --> 00:15:38.230
so you'll be on
your own for now.

302
00:15:38.230 --> 00:15:40.850
It's fine. Better to
get those kids home.

303
00:15:40.850 --> 00:15:43.150
I'll catch up to you guys later.

304
00:15:47.440 --> 00:15:48.700
[ACE]
You say you're not a captain,

305
00:15:48.700 --> 00:15:50.320
but there's no way
someone as strong as you

306
00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:52.240
would just hang around here.

307
00:15:52.240 --> 00:15:53.950
Gimme your worst!

308
00:15:53.950 --> 00:15:54.990
[YAMATO]
You want a fight?

309
00:15:54.990 --> 00:15:58.200
That's fine!
I was bored, anyway!

310
00:16:03.670 --> 00:16:06.670
[yells]

311
00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:11.220
Fire Fist!

312
00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:20.940
[yells]

313
00:16:24.730 --> 00:16:26.020
[both gasp]

314
00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:33.200
[ACE]
Something's up.

315
00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:36.200
If you're this strong, then why
aren't you going out to sea?

316
00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:40.250
It's his fault
that I'm stuck here.

317
00:16:42.070 --> 00:16:44.860
all because I was
born his child.

318
00:16:44.860 --> 00:16:48.560
Oh, really? So it's
all your father's fault?

319
00:16:48.560 --> 00:16:51.770
[ACE]
Aren't you just making excuses?

320
00:16:51.770 --> 00:16:53.270
[Yamato gasps]

321
00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:58.780
Everyone's the same.

322
00:16:58.780 --> 00:17:00.660
We can't choose our parents.

323
00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:01.900
You gotta make do.

324
00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:05.020
[YAMATO]
Do you think I'm stupid?

325
00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:07.130
You don't have to tell me that!

326
00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:09.250
You say you get it, but do you?

327
00:17:10.690 --> 00:17:13.180
You hate your father,
but you've given him power.

328
00:17:13.180 --> 00:17:15.780
He chained your hands,
but right now you're

329
00:17:15.780 --> 00:17:17.980
letting him chain
your heart, too!

330
00:17:18.410 --> 00:17:20.450
[Yamato gasps]

331
00:17:18.410 --> 00:17:20.700
[yells]

332
00:17:33.640 --> 00:17:36.640
[gasps]

333
00:17:36.640 --> 00:17:37.340
[ACE]
Yamato, why don't you
tell me what you really want?

334
00:17:37.340 --> 00:17:41.220
Yamato! Why don't you tell me
what you really want?

335
00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:44.070
[yells]

336
00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:49.570
[grunting]

337
00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:52.860
[cackles]

338
00:18:00.230 --> 00:18:03.400
[Yamato yelling]

339
00:18:14.040 --> 00:18:16.250
I understand now.

340
00:18:16.250 --> 00:18:19.170
Somewhere in my heart,
I've been holding myself back.

341
00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:23.370
Before I knew it,
I was afraid to even say it.

342
00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:26.920
That I want to sail the world
on a grand adventure!

343
00:18:26.920 --> 00:18:31.000
That I want to be like Oden
and live my life freely!

344
00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:34.300
I'll go to the sea.

345
00:18:34.300 --> 00:18:36.720
I'll find a way
off of this island!

346
00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:40.970
I'll find a way to be free,
just like I always dreamed!

347
00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:43.980
[Yamato gasps]

348
00:18:43.980 --> 00:18:45.810
Yeah! Now you're
talking, Yamato!

349
00:18:46.940 --> 00:18:49.360
[Ace yells]

350
00:18:51.110 --> 00:18:53.030
[Yamato gasps]

351
00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:01.740
[ACE]
Much better.

352
00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:04.830
Did that clear things up for ya?

353
00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:06.160
[gasps]

354
00:19:17.560 --> 00:19:21.980
[Ace laughs]
And he came home
all busted up again!

355
00:19:21.980 --> 00:19:23.060
[Ace sighs]

356
00:19:23.060 --> 00:19:24.230
I laugh, but he really gave me

357
00:19:24.230 --> 00:19:26.020
a lotta trouble
when we were kids!

358
00:19:24.560 --> 00:19:26.860
[yells]

359
00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:27.480
That little dope.

360
00:19:27.480 --> 00:19:29.690
[Yamato laughs]
Your brother
sounds like so much fun!

361
00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:30.650
Hell yeah!

362
00:19:30.650 --> 00:19:30.990
[giggles]
So. Who are
the top pirates right now?

363
00:19:30.990 --> 00:19:33.700
[giggles]
So who are the
top pirates right now?

364
00:19:33.700 --> 00:19:36.240
Is anyone our age making
a name for themselves?

365
00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:39.120
People our age? Let me think.

366
00:19:39.120 --> 00:19:42.290
The girls are crazy for
some Caven-something guy.

367
00:19:42.290 --> 00:19:43.500
[YAMATO]
Oh yeah?

368
00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:45.670
Well, nobody is on
my level just yet,

369
00:19:45.670 --> 00:19:45.710
but each sea has
their own tough guy

370
00:19:45.710 --> 00:19:47.580
but each sea has
their own tough guy.

371
00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:47.670
And one of them just might
make it big someday!

372
00:19:47.670 --> 00:19:50.090
and one of them just might
make it big someday!

373
00:19:50.090 --> 00:19:51.590
Like who, like who?

374
00:19:51.590 --> 00:19:54.800
[ACE]
Kid in the South Blue
and Law in the north

375
00:19:54.800 --> 00:19:56.600
and Bege in the west.

376
00:19:57.850 --> 00:19:58.400
[ACE]
But the toughest one
is gonna show up

377
00:19:58.400 --> 00:19:59.390
[ACE]
The toughest one is gonna
show up a few years from now,

378
00:19:59.390 --> 00:20:01.530
a few years from now,
and that's my brother!

379
00:20:01.530 --> 00:20:03.700
and that's my brother!

380
00:20:03.700 --> 00:20:04.780
[Yamato gasps]

381
00:20:04.060 --> 00:20:06.730
You'll see! He's gonna
make a big wave!

382
00:20:06.730 --> 00:20:07.940
Okay, I get it.

383
00:20:07.940 --> 00:20:09.900
You really love
this brother of yours!

384
00:20:09.900 --> 00:20:11.860
Yeah, so what?
You gotta problem?

385
00:20:11.860 --> 00:20:13.570
Ow, cut it out!

386
00:20:13.570 --> 00:20:15.610
How do you like it,
you stupid jerk?

387
00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:16.740
It hurts!

388
00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:20.540
[Ace, Yamato laughing]

389
00:20:21.180 --> 00:20:23.270
And as for this statue,
the truth is

390
00:20:23.270 --> 00:20:26.820
I'm the one who
attacked it first.

391
00:20:26.820 --> 00:20:28.400
[YAMATO]
But then Ace said

392
00:20:28.400 --> 00:20:31.110
"Tell Kaido that this is
a warning from me!

393
00:20:31.110 --> 00:20:32.320
I'll be back some day

394
00:20:32.320 --> 00:20:34.490
to give his real face
the same treatment!"

395
00:20:34.490 --> 00:20:35.700
[MOMONOSUKE]
I see.

396
00:20:35.700 --> 00:20:36.150
I did not know there
was a pirate who

397
00:20:36.150 --> 00:20:37.030
Everyone hold the line.

398
00:20:37.030 --> 00:20:39.870
tried to save the
Land of Wano in the past.

399
00:20:39.870 --> 00:20:42.370
[YAMATO]
My father was angry, of course,

400
00:20:42.370 --> 00:20:44.830
but in the end,
he never met Ace.

401
00:20:44.830 --> 00:20:46.630
[Momonosuke gasps]
Your father?

402
00:20:46.630 --> 00:20:47.920
That means...

403
00:20:47.920 --> 00:20:51.130
Oh, yeah. Did I not tell you
Kaido's my father?

404
00:20:51.130 --> 00:20:53.090
[both scream]

405
00:20:53.090 --> 00:20:55.010
[Yamato gasps]
Oh, no!

406
00:20:55.010 --> 00:20:57.220
C'mon, guys, you don't
have to be afraid of me!

407
00:20:57.220 --> 00:20:59.080
I hate Kaido! Even more
than you do, I bet!

408
00:20:59.080 --> 00:21:00.060
I'm getting there!

409
00:21:00.060 --> 00:21:01.980
I told you I'm Oden, right?

410
00:21:01.980 --> 00:21:03.520
[MOMONOSUKE]
That only
fills us with more doubt!

411
00:21:03.520 --> 00:21:05.190
Should I explain it again?

412
00:21:05.190 --> 00:21:06.900
Kaido's my enemy, okay?

413
00:21:06.900 --> 00:21:09.070
I dream of sailing
on a big adventure!

414
00:21:09.070 --> 00:21:11.440
I'm Oden, who only
wants to be free!

415
00:21:11.440 --> 00:21:13.240
Yes, sir. As you say.

416
00:21:13.240 --> 00:21:15.490
[MOMONOSUKE]
We are at
your mercy, mighty lord.

417
00:21:15.490 --> 00:21:16.780
[YAMATO]
Stop acting like that!

418
00:21:16.780 --> 00:21:17.950
We're friends, aren't we?

419
00:21:17.950 --> 00:21:19.530
But wait, Yamato.

420
00:21:19.530 --> 00:21:22.790
This man who tried to save the
Land of Wano, where is he now?

421
00:21:22.790 --> 00:21:25.950
[YAMATO]
Well, Ace died two years ago.

422
00:21:25.950 --> 00:21:27.210
[Momonosuke gasps]

423
00:21:27.210 --> 00:21:29.580
You knew Ace?
I didn't see that one coming!

424
00:21:29.580 --> 00:21:31.500
[OTAMA]
Yeah! We were best buddies!

425
00:21:31.500 --> 00:21:34.170
I've been working so hard
to become a kunoichi,

426
00:21:34.170 --> 00:21:36.670
waiting for him to
come back to see me.

427
00:21:36.670 --> 00:21:38.090
But mean ole Luffy
couldn't even

428
00:21:38.090 --> 00:21:39.460
break the news to me gently.

429
00:21:39.460 --> 00:21:41.260
Did the fire fix me?

430
00:21:41.260 --> 00:21:44.770
[LUFFY]
Ace is dead now.

431
00:21:44.770 --> 00:21:46.680
[OTAMA]
He just said it
out of the blue.

432
00:21:46.680 --> 00:21:49.310
It broke my heart
into a thousand pieces.

433
00:21:49.310 --> 00:21:52.320
Sorry. He can be
like that sometimes.

434
00:21:52.320 --> 00:21:53.780
He didn't mean to hurt you.

435
00:21:53.780 --> 00:21:55.480
But y'know, Otama

436
00:21:55.480 --> 00:21:58.070
Luffy's been through
a lot of pain, too.

437
00:21:58.070 --> 00:21:59.660
– It was tough.
– Huh?

438
00:21:59.660 --> 00:22:01.620
[Queen growls]

439
00:22:02.020 --> 00:22:04.230
Stop screwing up my party!

440
00:22:05.400 --> 00:22:08.400
[Beast Pirates gasp]

441
00:22:08.400 --> 00:22:11.900
Yo, losers!
Pluck that turkey's wings!

442
00:22:12.640 --> 00:22:15.720
Don't just stand there,
kill that bozo!

443
00:22:15.720 --> 00:22:17.050
[Beast Pirat K gasps]

444
00:22:17.050 --> 00:22:18.220
Doesn't seem right.

445
00:22:18.220 --> 00:22:20.180
I mean, that guy
saved our lives!

446
00:22:20.180 --> 00:22:21.390
Yeah. I know.

447
00:22:21.390 --> 00:22:23.930
But the boss will
kill us if we disobey!

448
00:22:23.930 --> 00:22:25.090
[Beast Pirat K gasps]

449
00:22:25.090 --> 00:22:27.460
Do you want me to
smash your heads in?

450
00:22:27.460 --> 00:22:30.130
Now get your asses in there!

451
00:22:31.230 --> 00:22:35.030
[Beast Pirates yell]

452
00:22:35.030 --> 00:22:36.700
[MARCO]
To be honest,
I wasn't planning on

453
00:22:36.700 --> 00:22:39.160
going after Kaido, myself.

454
00:22:39.160 --> 00:22:39.990
[Robin, Brook gasp]

455
00:22:39.990 --> 00:22:41.780
Nico Robin! Mister Bones!

456
00:22:41.780 --> 00:22:45.580
Do what you gotta do!
Run to the castle!

457
00:22:45.580 --> 00:22:46.780
That's fine with me.

458
00:22:46.780 --> 00:22:48.790
If you insist, then we're off!

459
00:22:48.790 --> 00:22:50.870
You're gonna suffer, Marco!

460
00:22:50.870 --> 00:22:52.960
[cackles]

461
00:22:58.670 --> 00:23:00.460
Thought you could
take all of us, huh?

462
00:23:00.460 --> 00:23:02.880
You walked straight
into your grave!

463
00:23:11.220 --> 00:23:13.090
[gasps]

464
00:23:13.090 --> 00:23:14.890
You guys ready?

465
00:23:14.890 --> 00:23:16.640
Let's do this!

466
00:23:22.400 --> 00:23:25.150
[Beast Pirates scream]

467
00:23:34.910 --> 00:23:37.950
C'mon, now how is that fair?

468
00:23:37.950 --> 00:23:39.700
This is great!

469
00:23:39.700 --> 00:23:42.660
[MARCO]
You're about to face off
with an Emperor, you know!

470
00:23:42.660 --> 00:23:44.580
You're not nervous at all?

471
00:23:44.580 --> 00:23:45.750
[ZORO]
Of course not.

472
00:23:45.750 --> 00:23:47.250
What good would that do?

473
00:23:47.250 --> 00:23:50.920
My captain gives the order
and I follow. Simple as that.

474
00:23:50.920 --> 00:23:53.380
[MARCO]
I'm counting on
Straw Hat to pull through,

475
00:23:53.380 --> 00:23:57.560
and not just him, everyone
from the Worst Generation.

476
00:23:58.930 --> 00:24:00.180
[MARCO]
I wonder what Ace would've said

477
00:24:00.180 --> 00:24:01.890
if he knew his brother
was picking a fight

478
00:24:01.890 --> 00:24:04.400
with an Emperor of the Sea.

479
00:24:04.400 --> 00:24:07.320
I'm begging. C'mon!

480
00:24:07.320 --> 00:24:10.190
I said no. Now drop it!

481
00:24:12.150 --> 00:24:15.320
[WHITEBEARD]
How many times
do we have to go over this?

482
00:24:15.320 --> 00:24:18.080
I told you who the Second
Division Commander was

483
00:24:18.080 --> 00:24:20.120
before you, didn't I?

484
00:24:20.120 --> 00:24:20.770
And I told you why
the position was vacant?

485
00:24:20.770 --> 00:24:23.030
And you kept his
position vacant.

486
00:24:23.030 --> 00:24:26.360
Wano's isolationist policy
played a part in that, too.

487
00:24:26.360 --> 00:24:27.860
We didn't know.

488
00:24:27.860 --> 00:24:31.410
In other words,
since no info got in or out,

489
00:24:31.410 --> 00:24:34.330
it was years before
we heard Lord Oden died.

490
00:24:35.020 --> 00:24:38.140
We thought about forcing our way
into Wano and starting a fight,

491
00:24:38.140 --> 00:24:41.020
but there's a hundred different
ways that plan could go south.

492
00:24:41.020 --> 00:24:44.110
Win or lose,
it'd take a heavy toll.

493
00:24:44.110 --> 00:24:45.940
Y'think so?

494
00:24:46.340 --> 00:24:49.840
Fine! Then why don't you
let me go alone?

495
00:24:49.840 --> 00:24:52.260
[giggles]

496
00:24:52.260 --> 00:24:54.410
[ACE]
I made a promise.

497
00:24:54.410 --> 00:24:58.500
Even Kozuki Oden
couldn't defeat Kaido.

498
00:25:02.790 --> 00:25:05.760
[WHITEBEARD]
Don't overestimate yourself!

499
00:25:05.760 --> 00:25:07.920
He'd crush you! Now sit down!

500
00:25:07.920 --> 00:25:08.960
[gasps]

501
00:25:08.960 --> 00:25:10.430
[thudding]

502
00:25:20.620 --> 00:25:23.980
[laughs]
Yeah, I remember
how strong that Oden guy was!

503
00:25:23.980 --> 00:25:25.820
But I know how you feel, Ace.

504
00:25:25.820 --> 00:25:29.030
We're all searching
for fame. For glory.

505
00:25:29.030 --> 00:25:31.360
It's not always about that.

506
00:25:31.360 --> 00:25:34.830
You don't get it, Teach.
Ace isn't looking for a prize.

507
00:25:36.240 --> 00:25:37.370
[ACE]
Damn it.

508
00:25:37.370 --> 00:25:38.540
Hm?

509
00:25:38.540 --> 00:25:40.660
[Teach laughs]

510
00:25:40.660 --> 00:25:42.880
[ACE]
I have to get stronger.

511
00:25:42.880 --> 00:25:45.280
I have to keep my promise!

512
00:25:45.280 --> 00:25:48.240
That's a heavy weight
you decided to carry, Ace.

513
00:25:48.240 --> 00:25:49.830
I'm just saying.

514
00:25:49.830 --> 00:25:52.540
So if Pops ever
lets you go, call me.

515
00:25:52.540 --> 00:25:54.710
I'd be happy to
fight by your side.

516
00:25:54.710 --> 00:25:57.420
You can count me in, too.

517
00:25:57.420 --> 00:26:00.340
Oh yeah? Then we can win, easy.

518
00:26:00.340 --> 00:26:01.760
[gasps]

519
00:26:02.630 --> 00:26:05.760
[MARCO]
A little optimism
is good, but come on.

520
00:26:05.760 --> 00:26:08.180
[laughs]

521
00:26:18.970 --> 00:26:21.270
[QUEEN]
Come on, Marco,
you don't really think

522
00:26:21.270 --> 00:26:24.060
we're just gonna stand here
and let you fly away!

523
00:26:23.390 --> 00:26:29.070
<b>Superstar Queen
Ancient Saur-Saur Fruit: Brachiosaurus</b>

524
00:26:24.060 --> 00:26:27.570
Besides, all those samurai
are probably dead!

525
00:26:27.570 --> 00:26:29.690
Why even bother?

526
00:26:29.690 --> 00:26:31.490
[KING]
Once we finish off Oden's son,

527
00:26:31.490 --> 00:26:33.070
this fight will be over.

528
00:26:33.070 --> 00:26:36.370
He will die along with the
old Wano, and from its ashes,

529
00:26:34.280 --> 00:26:39.700
<b>Superstar King
Ancient Saur-Saur Fruit: Pteranodon</b>

530
00:26:36.370 --> 00:26:40.120
the pirate empire of
New Onigashima will be born!

531
00:26:40.120 --> 00:26:41.910
[MARCO]
You really think it's that easy?

532
00:26:41.910 --> 00:26:43.830
You're in for a rude awakening!

533
00:26:43.830 --> 00:26:46.710
[QUEEN]
Shut yer trap, bird brain!

534
00:26:52.760 --> 00:26:55.340
[QUEEN]
Damn it!
What kind of power is that?

535
00:26:55.340 --> 00:26:57.470
Is this guy invincible?

536
00:26:58.640 --> 00:26:59.890
[MARCO]
Be careful.

537
00:26:59.890 --> 00:27:02.560
You guys are facing
a new generation now!

538
00:27:02.560 --> 00:27:05.230
[QUEEN]
The Beast Pirates
will destroy you

539
00:27:05.230 --> 00:27:08.440
and dominate the new era!

540
00:27:10.640 --> 00:27:12.350
[King gasps]

541
00:27:11.480 --> 00:27:14.110
[Marco grunts]

542
00:27:17.410 --> 00:27:19.160
[QUEEN]
Dammit!

543
00:27:21.200 --> 00:27:24.620
[ZORO]
Marco, forget
these losers, let's go!

544
00:27:24.620 --> 00:27:24.860
[MARCO]
Get ready. On three.

545
00:27:24.860 --> 00:27:26.000
I wasn't ready!

546
00:27:26.000 --> 00:27:28.330
– What?
– Three!

547
00:27:28.330 --> 00:27:30.460
[Zoro yells]

548
00:27:29.240 --> 00:27:31.750
[Queen grunts]

549
00:27:50.330 --> 00:27:52.920
Um, yeah. I thought you knew.

550
00:27:52.920 --> 00:27:55.460
Like I said,
he kinda sounded cold

551
00:27:55.460 --> 00:27:58.300
when he talked about his death.

552
00:27:58.300 --> 00:28:00.140
But Ace is dead now.

553
00:28:00.140 --> 00:28:01.070
jerk!

554
00:28:00.340 --> 00:28:01.120
[sobbing]

555
00:28:01.120 --> 00:28:02.320
I was the jerk!

556
00:28:02.320 --> 00:28:04.540
I said awful things to Luffy!

557
00:28:03.090 --> 00:28:07.720
[cries]

558
00:28:04.580 --> 00:28:06.000
I wouldn't worry,

559
00:28:06.000 --> 00:28:09.710
that's just Luffy being Luffy,
it'll be okay!

560
00:28:09.710 --> 00:28:10.790
Yeah, but...

561
00:28:11.100 --> 00:28:15.440
Big Bro! I gotta
tell him I'm sorry!

562
00:28:15.440 --> 00:28:18.070
I told you not to worry, right?

563
00:28:16.940 --> 00:28:18.150
[Otama gasps]

564
00:28:18.150 --> 00:28:20.030
Well, anyway,
we should work on that plan

565
00:28:20.030 --> 00:28:20.400
We all know

566
00:28:20.400 --> 00:28:22.070
you came up with, Otama!

567
00:28:22.070 --> 00:28:23.610
I know you got this!

568
00:28:25.810 --> 00:28:27.810
<b>Forbidden

Storehouse



Inside

the Dome</b>

569
00:28:28.060 --> 00:28:34.810
Huh? W-Wait, so Roger had a son,
and he's Luffy's brother?

570
00:28:34.810 --> 00:28:36.860
That's quite
the friend you made!

571
00:28:36.860 --> 00:28:39.530
[YAMATO]
Yeah. Can you believe it?

572
00:28:39.530 --> 00:28:42.570
Without knowing that,
you brought Luffy to Wano!

573
00:28:42.570 --> 00:28:44.410
[MOMONOSUKE]
Indeed we did.

574
00:28:44.410 --> 00:28:47.370
Pirates are as numerous
as stars in the sky,

575
00:28:47.370 --> 00:28:48.950
and yet you met him.

576
00:28:48.950 --> 00:28:51.700
Ace's promise will
finally come true.

577
00:28:51.700 --> 00:28:54.920
This can't be
anything but destiny!

578
00:28:56.580 --> 00:28:58.880
[YAMATO]
I mean,
the answer's in front of us.

579
00:28:58.880 --> 00:29:00.420
The will of "D."

580
00:29:00.420 --> 00:29:02.680
It's right there
in Luffy's name!

581
00:29:02.680 --> 00:29:03.920
[gasps]

582
00:29:08.600 --> 00:29:12.140
[Big Mom cackles]

583
00:29:12.140 --> 00:29:13.600
[grunts]

584
00:29:18.460 --> 00:29:20.790
[laughs]
Yummy!

585
00:29:23.570 --> 00:29:26.200
Oh yeah, tasty!

586
00:29:28.780 --> 00:29:31.700
[Zeus chewing]

587
00:29:31.700 --> 00:29:34.120
[ZEUS]
Now that's a snack!

588
00:29:37.690 --> 00:29:39.960
[ZEUS]
Good! I was so hungry!

589
00:29:39.960 --> 00:29:45.130
But now I'm full.
Full of raw power.

590
00:29:45.130 --> 00:29:47.140
You boys enjoy your meal?

591
00:29:47.140 --> 00:29:48.680
Yes, Mama!

592
00:29:48.680 --> 00:29:50.680
I'm good to go!

593
00:29:52.470 --> 00:29:55.100
[BIG MOM]
Well, time's a wastin'!

594
00:29:59.580 --> 00:30:00.880
[Kaido sighs]

595
00:30:00.880 --> 00:30:06.130
[cackles]

596
00:30:06.130 --> 00:30:09.360
[BIG MOM]
Straw Hat still hasn't shown up?

597
00:30:09.360 --> 00:30:11.070
Here's the deal, Kaido!

598
00:30:11.070 --> 00:30:13.530
Kill as many of the
Straw Hats as you like,

599
00:30:13.530 --> 00:30:16.950
but Miss Nico Robin
is coming with me.

600
00:30:16.950 --> 00:30:18.580
Why do you need her?

601
00:30:18.580 --> 00:30:21.460
Can't your three-eyed daughter
read the ancient text as well?

602
00:30:21.460 --> 00:30:24.250
Y'mean Pudding? I don't know!

603
00:30:24.250 --> 00:30:27.500
Her True Eye hasn't awakened.
She's too damn slow!

604
00:30:25.250 --> 00:30:27.550
[Beast Pirates scream]

605
00:30:27.550 --> 00:30:31.550
Fine. Have it your way, then.

606
00:30:31.020 --> 00:30:34.190
<b>5th Floor

Inside the Castle</b>

607
00:30:32.510 --> 00:30:33.640
[gasps]

608
00:30:34.840 --> 00:30:36.180
Humble though our
strength may be,

609
00:30:36.180 --> 00:30:37.970
we have held this staircase.

610
00:30:37.970 --> 00:30:39.260
Proceed this way.

611
00:30:38.890 --> 00:30:41.270
[yells]

612
00:30:39.300 --> 00:30:42.310
It shall lead you-gara
to the castle roof.

613
00:30:41.310 --> 00:30:45.730
[groans]

614
00:30:42.350 --> 00:30:44.520
Wow, thanks, Lion Viper!

615
00:30:44.520 --> 00:30:45.980
[SHISHILIAN]
It's Shishilian.

616
00:30:45.980 --> 00:30:48.400
I won't forget how
you helped Raizo!

617
00:30:48.400 --> 00:30:49.690
You guys are really brave,

618
00:30:49.690 --> 00:30:52.440
so promise me
you'll hang in there.

619
00:30:52.440 --> 00:30:55.570
Don't you worry,
I'll handle Kaido.

620
00:30:55.570 --> 00:30:57.950
[Minks cheering]

621
00:31:00.870 --> 00:31:04.330
[BIG MOM]
Now, where exactly
are you gonna drop this island?

622
00:31:04.330 --> 00:31:05.830
[KAIDO]
In the middle of the capital.

623
00:31:05.830 --> 00:31:08.330
There's a castle there
that symbolizes the Kozuki.

624
00:31:10.250 --> 00:31:13.800
[laughs]
You're not concerned
about all the casualties?

625
00:31:13.800 --> 00:31:15.840
They're having a festival,
aren't they?

626
00:31:15.840 --> 00:31:17.220
That a joke?

627
00:31:17.220 --> 00:31:20.010
Y'think slaves are
that hard to come by?

628
00:31:21.520 --> 00:31:22.930
[sighs]

629
00:31:24.020 --> 00:31:26.940
[KAIDO]
The new capital
will be a sight to behold.

630
00:31:26.940 --> 00:31:29.440
[Kaido cackles]

631
00:31:29.440 --> 00:31:31.610
Oh! Is that where it's hidden?

632
00:31:31.610 --> 00:31:34.150
The Road Poneglyph?

633
00:31:34.150 --> 00:31:37.110
You're not even trying
to hide your true intentions!

634
00:31:37.110 --> 00:31:40.580
Oh, get over it!
This isn't some battle of wits!

635
00:31:40.580 --> 00:31:42.080
Even after all this time,

636
00:31:42.080 --> 00:31:44.710
you're still like
a little brother to me!

637
00:31:44.710 --> 00:31:46.880
That said, let me remind you.

638
00:31:46.880 --> 00:31:49.750
That day in God Valley,
when Rocks came to an end,

639
00:31:49.750 --> 00:31:54.300
it was me who gave you
the Mythical Fish-Fish Fruit!

640
00:31:54.300 --> 00:31:58.010
That's a debt you'll owe
for the rest of your life.

641
00:31:58.010 --> 00:32:00.260
[KAIDO]
Say what you like.

642
00:32:00.260 --> 00:32:03.140
[Big Mom chuckles]

643
00:32:05.350 --> 00:32:08.400
[KAIDO]
We'll settle this
after we get our treasure.

644
00:32:08.240 --> 00:32:10.910
Let's get the One Piece!

645
00:32:08.400 --> 00:32:11.020
[BOTH]
The One Piece, that is!
